1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,457
It is five thirty in the morning and I
have not moved for three hours.

2
00:00:04,477 --> 00:00:05,870
Not my legs.

3
00:00:05,890 --> 00:00:07,403
Not my hands.

4
00:00:07,423 --> 00:00:09,897
My mother is in the chair by my window.

5
00:00:09,917 --> 00:00:12,813
My father is propped against the foot of
my bed.

6
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:17,374
Both of them are turned to face me, and
both of their mouths are open.

7
00:00:17,394 --> 00:00:20,943
The smell of blood in here is so strong I
can taste it.

8
00:00:20,963 --> 00:00:23,942
Neither of them has blinked since I woke
up.

9
00:00:23,962 --> 00:00:27,174
The thing that put them there has not left
this room.

10
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:30,310
If it finds out I am awake, I die in this
bed, and

11
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:33,645
there is nobody left in this house to stop
it.

12
00:00:33,665 --> 00:00:35,280
Let us go back to the beginning.

13
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:39,503
Three hours ago I was asleep, like any
other night.

14
00:00:39,523 --> 00:00:42,827
The last thing I remember before all of it
is my mother

15
00:00:42,847 --> 00:00:45,997
at my door with the landing light behind
her.

16
00:00:46,017 --> 00:00:49,850
"Lights out, love. I do not want to hear
that tablet at midnight."

17
00:00:49,870 --> 00:00:53,476
And my father, further down the hall, not
even coming in.

18
00:00:53,496 --> 00:00:56,298
"Door is locked, mate. Go to sleep."

19
00:00:56,318 --> 00:00:58,964
He checked the locks every night of my
life.

20
00:00:58,984 --> 00:01:02,118
I need you to know that he checked them
that night too.

21
00:01:02,138 --> 00:01:07,860
At 2:20 I woke up because somebody was
screaming on the other side of the house.

22
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:09,073
Not a shout.

23
00:01:09,093 --> 00:01:10,282
Not a word.

24
00:01:10,302 --> 00:01:15,255
A long high scream that stopped in the
middle, like a door had been closed on it.

25
00:01:15,275 --> 00:01:19,320
This is a retelling, inspired by a story
told online.

26
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:20,409
I sat up.

27
00:01:20,429 --> 00:01:21,970
I got to my door.

28
00:01:21,990 --> 00:01:25,539
I want that on the record, because of what
I did next.

29
00:01:25,559 --> 00:01:28,588
You are twelve years old and somebody just
screamed.

30
00:01:28,608 --> 00:01:31,719
Do you go and look, or do you use the
bathroom first?

31
00:01:32,319 --> 00:01:34,909
My body told me something very stupid.

32
00:01:34,929 --> 00:01:36,621
I needed the toilet.

33
00:01:36,641 --> 00:01:41,761
Somebody had screamed in my house, and I
turned left into the bathroom first.

34
00:01:41,781 --> 00:01:45,198
I have had three hours to think about
those three minutes.

35
00:01:45,218 --> 00:01:46,736
I put the light on.

36
00:01:46,756 --> 00:01:48,279
I remember the light.

37
00:01:48,299 --> 00:01:51,705
It was the last normal thing that ever
happened to me.

38
00:01:51,725 --> 00:01:54,368
I washed my hands, because that is what
you

39
00:01:54,388 --> 00:01:57,482
do, even at half past two, even after
that.

40
00:01:57,502 --> 00:02:01,726
Then I turned the light off, opened the
door a crack, and looked out at the hall.

41
00:02:02,326 --> 00:02:04,246
There was blood on the carpet.

42
00:02:04,266 --> 00:02:05,451
Not a drop.

43
00:02:05,471 --> 00:02:06,458
A smear.

44
00:02:06,478 --> 00:02:10,012
A wide dark one that started at the far
end by my parents'

45
00:02:10,032 --> 00:02:13,587
room and went all the way to the top of
the stairs.

46
00:02:13,607 --> 00:02:16,495
Something heavy had been pulled along that
carpet.

47
00:02:16,515 --> 00:02:18,770
The front door was down those stairs.

48
00:02:18,790 --> 00:02:22,491
Twelve steps, the hall, one latch, and
then the street, and the

49
00:02:22,511 --> 00:02:26,308
Kellys across the road with their bedroom
light still on.

50
00:02:26,328 --> 00:02:28,492
I did not go down the stairs.

51
00:02:28,512 --> 00:02:30,003
Blood on the carpet.

52
00:02:30,023 --> 00:02:32,345
The front door is twelve steps away.

53
00:02:32,365 --> 00:02:34,952
Do you run for it, or hide in your bed?

54
00:02:34,972 --> 00:02:39,233
I went back into my room, got into my bed,
and pulled the sheets over

55
00:02:39,253 --> 00:02:43,901
my head like a seven-year-old, as if that
does anything to anything.

56
00:02:43,921 --> 00:02:47,206
I lay under there and told myself I was
dreaming.

57
00:02:47,226 --> 00:02:49,316
I kept that up for about eight minutes.

58
00:02:49,916 --> 00:02:52,438
Then my bedroom door creaked open.

59
00:02:52,458 --> 00:02:55,300
And because something in me needed to
know, I pulled

60
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:57,952
the blanket down off one eye and looked.

61
00:02:57,972 --> 00:03:02,551
It was bent over in my doorway, and it was
far too tall for my room.

62
00:03:02,571 --> 00:03:03,851
It was hairless.

63
00:03:03,871 --> 00:03:04,889
All of it.

64
00:03:04,909 --> 00:03:08,312
Nothing on its head, no eyebrows, nothing
anywhere.

65
00:03:08,332 --> 00:03:09,759
It had no eyes.

66
00:03:09,779 --> 00:03:12,388
I do not mean shut, or white, or hidden.

67
00:03:12,408 --> 00:03:17,299
There was nothing on its face where eyes
go, and nothing where a mouth goes either.

68
00:03:17,319 --> 00:03:21,267
A smooth pale plate, hanging lower than
its own shoulders.

69
00:03:21,287 --> 00:03:23,237
It wore nothing at all.

70
00:03:23,257 --> 00:03:26,828
It moved like something that was never
taught to stand up,

71
00:03:26,848 --> 00:03:30,621
back slouched right over, arms hanging
past its knees.

72
00:03:30,641 --> 00:03:33,605
And it was dragging my mother and my
father into

73
00:03:33,625 --> 00:03:36,174
my bedroom by the arms, one in each hand.

74
00:03:36,774 --> 00:03:38,286
It was not stupid.

75
00:03:38,306 --> 00:03:41,291
That is the part I need you to understand.

76
00:03:41,311 --> 00:03:45,730
A thing that walks like that should not
have been able to do what it did next.

77
00:03:45,750 --> 00:03:49,144
It propped my father against the foot of
my bed, sitting up,

78
00:03:49,164 --> 00:03:52,666
and turned his face until he was looking
at my pillow.

79
00:03:52,686 --> 00:03:57,745
Then it lifted my mother into the chair by
my window and turned her the same way.

80
00:03:57,765 --> 00:03:59,103
It arranged them.

81
00:03:59,123 --> 00:04:00,596
Like a photograph.

82
00:04:00,616 --> 00:04:03,772
Like something that wanted the picture to
come out right.

83
00:04:03,792 --> 00:04:08,305
Then it put both hands flat on my wall and
started dragging them along it.

84
00:04:08,325 --> 00:04:09,656
It drew a circle.

85
00:04:09,676 --> 00:04:13,694
Then a star inside the circle, upside
down, five points, the kind

86
00:04:13,714 --> 00:04:17,622
of thing boys scratch on the back of their
school books.

87
00:04:17,642 --> 00:04:19,731
It was painting with my parents.

88
00:04:19,751 --> 00:04:24,065
And then it stepped back from the wall,
the way you step back from a drawing.

89
00:04:24,085 --> 00:04:26,352
Then it wrote something under the circle.

90
00:04:26,372 --> 00:04:30,660
One line of letters, pulled across my
wallpaper with one finger.

91
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,042
It was too dark.

92
00:04:32,062 --> 00:04:33,692
I could not read it.

93
00:04:33,712 --> 00:04:38,673
And then it got down on my floor, folded
itself up, and went under my bed.

94
00:04:38,693 --> 00:04:39,984
Under my bed.

95
00:04:40,004 --> 00:04:41,319
With me on top of it.

96
00:04:41,919 --> 00:04:43,827
That was three hours ago.

97
00:04:43,847 --> 00:04:47,005
Here is the thing about lying still for
three hours.

98
00:04:47,025 --> 00:04:49,349
Your eyes get better at the dark.

99
00:04:49,369 --> 00:04:51,923
The clock on my table says 5:30.

100
00:04:51,943 --> 00:04:54,416
My window has gone from black to grey.

101
00:04:54,436 --> 00:04:58,946
And the writing on my wall has been
getting clearer for about twenty minutes.

102
00:04:58,966 --> 00:05:00,717
I have not looked at it.

103
00:05:00,737 --> 00:05:03,613
I have been looking at my father instead,
because he

104
00:05:03,633 --> 00:05:06,904
is the only thing in this room that cannot
hurt me.

105
00:05:06,924 --> 00:05:09,542
I have one plan and it is a bad one.

106
00:05:09,562 --> 00:05:11,506
The door is nine feet away.

107
00:05:11,526 --> 00:05:14,371
I run, I take the stairs, I get the latch,
and

108
00:05:14,391 --> 00:05:17,624
I scream until the Kellys put their light
on.

109
00:05:17,644 --> 00:05:18,811
Nine feet.

110
00:05:18,831 --> 00:05:20,585
And it is under the bed.

111
00:05:20,605 --> 00:05:23,028
I would have to put my feet on the floor.

112
00:05:23,048 --> 00:05:24,616
Nine feet to the door.

113
00:05:24,636 --> 00:05:26,245
It is under the bed.

114
00:05:26,265 --> 00:05:28,281
Do you stay still, or run?

115
00:05:28,301 --> 00:05:32,602
So I have been doing the only thing I can
do, which is nothing at all.

116
00:05:32,622 --> 00:05:33,879
Breathing slow.

117
00:05:33,899 --> 00:05:35,622
Keeping my face soft.

118
00:05:35,642 --> 00:05:39,813
Not blinking too much, because I read once
that they can tell.

119
00:05:39,833 --> 00:05:41,955
"It does not know I am awake."

120
00:05:41,975 --> 00:05:45,070
I have been saying that to myself for
three hours.

121
00:05:45,090 --> 00:05:47,269
I am going to read the wall now.

122
00:05:47,289 --> 00:05:48,751
I do not want to.

123
00:05:48,771 --> 00:05:52,610
But I would rather know what it says than
die next to it not knowing.

124
00:05:53,210 --> 00:05:54,885
So I move my eyes.

125
00:05:54,905 --> 00:05:56,176
Not my head.

126
00:05:56,196 --> 00:06:00,954
Just my eyes, right, to the circle and the
star and the line underneath it.

127
00:06:00,974 --> 00:06:02,773
And my eyes have adjusted.

128
00:06:02,793 --> 00:06:04,332
And I can read it.

129
00:06:04,352 --> 00:06:06,436
It says: I know you're awake.

130
00:06:06,456 --> 00:06:08,978
Under the bed, something shifts its
weight.

131
00:06:08,998 --> 00:06:11,957
It was never waiting to find out if I woke
up.

132
00:06:11,977 --> 00:06:16,091
It wrote that before I opened my eyes,
because it already knew.

133
00:06:16,111 --> 00:06:19,132
It has been waiting three hours for me to
read it.

134
00:06:19,152 --> 00:06:22,658
If you were in that bed, would you have
stayed still, or run for the door?

